  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through Sunday)\nIssued at 150 PM CDT Mon Jul 27 2026\n\nThe upper level high remains in place over the southern Plains\nthrough the end of the week. Therefore no change is expected in\nthe weather with temperatures near the century mark. Thankfully\nthe high is centered far enough north that easterly flow dampens\nthe heat enough to prevent a run of truly brutal temperatures.\n\nThe pattern changes slightly by the weekend. The high amplifies\nand shifts slightly back to the west allowing a trough to drop\ndown into the upper Midwest. This trough pushes a front south into\nour CWA Saturday and long term models are showing convection\ndeveloping along the front. We will still be under the upper\ninfluence of the high so subsidence should prevent widespread\nconvection, but perhaps we will see some isolated\nactivity...enough to break the monotony of this week. The NBM\nindicates that a northeasterly wind shift will not do much if\nanything to cool temperatures so we will have to see if this\nchanges over the several models runs.\n\nHennig",
